---
const title = "Math Drill Web";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="A browser-based mental arithmetic trainer." />
    <title>{title}</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <p class="eyebrow">Math Drill</p>
      <h1>Practice arithmetic. Find the patterns.</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        A browser version of the timed arithmetic trainer is coming here. It will
        preserve the desktop session format while adding local insights and
        adaptive practice.
      </p>
      <div class="status" role="status">
        <strong>Web foundation ready.</strong>
        <span>Interactive drill work begins with W01.</span>
      </div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :global(*) { box-sizing: border-box; }
  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    min-width: 320px;
    background: #f5f1e8;
    color: #1f2a24;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
  }
  main { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 18vh 24px; }
  .eyebrow { color: #66765e; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  h1 { max-width: 12ch; margin: 16px 0; font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 8vw, 5.6rem); line-height: .95; }
  .intro { max-width: 58ch; color: #526056; font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .status { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 16px; margin-top: 40px; padding: 18px; border-left: 4px solid #c86b3c; background: #fffaf0; }
</style>
